<% content_for :header do %>
  Your Copilot account has been upgraded to GitHub Enterprise
<% end %>

<p>
  Your Copilot Business for non–GitHub Enterprise (CBfnGHE) account, <%= @business.name %>,
  has been upgraded to a full GitHub Enterprise account as part of our migration.
</p>

<%= render(Mail::RowComponent.new) do %>
  <%= render(Mail::ColumnComponent.new) do %>
    <ul>
      <li>Your existing Copilot licenses, policies, and billing are unchanged; your users can continue using Copilot as they do today.</li>

      <li>You can now create organizations and repositories under your enterprise.</li>

      <li>When you add members to an organization, those users will consume GitHub Enterprise licenses. Copilot users who are assigned at the enterprise level only and are not members of any organization do not consume GitHub Enterprise licenses—they remain Copilot‑only users.</li>

      <li>Leveraging more of the GitHub platform — for example, using organizations and repositories — will unlock more advanced Copilot capabilities, such as repository‑aware Copilot Chat and Copilot agents that can work directly with your code and projects.</li>
    </ul>
  <% end %>
<% end %>

<br>

<p>
  If you have questions about your GitHub Enterprise account or Copilot licensing, please contact your GitHub account representative or
  <a href="<%= contact_url %>">Support</a>.
</p>

<% content_for :footer_text do %>
  You’re receiving this email because you’re an owner of the <strong><%= @business.name %></strong>
  enterprise on GitHub.
<% end %>
